# A chain (sites 1 to 5) feeds the middle row of a strip three pillars wide (sites 6 to 17). The last pillar of the chain must fire a pillar that loses light to three other neighbours, and fails.
# Reference: the same network integrated independently (complex arithmetic, LSODA).
title Chain into strip at coupling 0.043: blocked
sites 5
path 1 5 kappa=0.043
grid 4 3 kappa=0.043
link 5 10 kappa=0.043
kick 1 amplitude=2
run 2500
expect total 5
expect last 231.34194 0.003
expect count 1 1
expect arrival 1 12.77173 0.003
expect peak 1 58.401923 2e-4
expect count 5 1
expect arrival 5 231.34194 0.003
expect peak 5 55.360062 2e-4
expect count 10 0
expect count 13 0
expect each 1 5 1
expect silent 6 17
